      "id": 1,
      "text": "Irwin was founded in 1888 by Charles Dixon and the Higham brothers, who claimed land in what would become Swan Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/irwin_idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Shoshone and Bannock tribes hunted and gathered in the Swan Valley during summer months.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/irwin_idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "French trappers first explored the area in the early 19th century, followed by American trappers around 1810.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/irwin_idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Conant Valley, part of Swan Valley, is named after Charles Conant, a mid‑19th‑century trapper.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/irwin_idaho",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Irwin sits along the Snake River, a key waterway that feeds Palisades Reservoir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/irwin_idaho",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, Irwin’s economy thrives on tourism, offering RV spaces, cabins, and fishing on the Snake River.",
